
# <type>(<scope>)!: <summary>   -> max 72 chars (aim for 50), imperative,
#                                   lowercase, no period. '!' = breaking.
#   "If applied, this commit will <summary>"
#
# Body (required for feat, fix, perf, refactor, revert): wrap at 72.
#   - Why is this change needed? What was wrong before?
#   - What changes in behavior? Side effects, alternatives discarded.
#   - Evidence for prompt/model/tool changes: eval before/after
#     (accuracy, cost, latency).
#
# Trailers (optional, one per line, after a blank line):
#   Refs: #12 | Fixes: #12 | BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks + migration>
#
# Types: feat fix perf refactor test eval docs build ci chore revert
# Scopes: agents alerts budget cli deps evals graph hooks infra k8s llm
#         middleware postmortem prompts rbac scenarios slack tools
